"</div>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ansel __is not__ a hobby project. It is a working tool designed to get job done, and\n"
"[the pact](./contribute/pact.md) commits it to responsibilities a hobby never carries.\n"
"Funding is your side of that pact: the project answers for your needs; its workers'\n"
"conditions are, in return, partly yours. What is the difference with a hobby project?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/donate.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Chores"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:35
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Planning for long-term maintenance, stability and robustness implies doing chores, like\n"
"refactoring code, simplifying the programming structure, and identifying what features need\n"
"to be pruned. In addition of being tedious, these chores are often unpleasant, as they\n"
"don't involve any creativity and don't produce any cool new feature that will boost\n"
"marketing, but often require to understand some tangled and messy code written as someone\n"
"else's Saturday project.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It's just boring responsible management, yet time-consuming. But someone needs to do it —\n"
"and it is precisely the work that never gets rewarded by applause, which is why it must be\n"
"rewarded by something else.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Array Element: tags
#: content/donate.md:40
#: content/news/modules-groups-redesign/index.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Design"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:45
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Design is what happens when you search for the simplest, minimalist, solution to somebody's\n"
"problem. Design requires the designer to understand the problem from the human perspective,\n"
"and to know the available technologies well enough to find out the most suited one.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:52
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The opposite of design is blindly \"adding support for …\", which implies you cram your\n"
"application with as many features as you can, until you can't maintain it anymore and you\n"
"move on to the next project. This is called\n"
"[feature creep](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feature_creep) and its effect on people is\n"
"called [feature fatigue](https://www.jstor.org/stable/30162393). It harms both projects and\n"
"people.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here again, the task is time-consuming, in addition of requiring a special set of skills\n"
"(_engineering_) that require time themselves to master. It goes way beyond the mere ability\n"
"to write code, most of it actually happens before any code is written, and when properly\n"
"done, it also reduces the amount of code needed, thus helping maintainability.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/donate.md:58
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Overhead"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:65
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The product is never the product, the product is always the service in which the product is\n"
"a key component. Delivering some software as an installable executable is not so hard.\n"
"Thinking that alone brings value to people is being deluded. Providing user support in a\n"
"timely manner, user education and debugging is the hardest part, as it is a recurring task\n"
"and a cognitive load, but that is required so users can actually get the job done.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/donate.md:66
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Responsible management"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:69
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ansel has:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:78
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- a developer [documentation](https://dev.ansel.photos/) to help contributors avoid\n"
"  reverse-engineering the code and to help long-term maintenance,\n"
"- automatic [camera support](./resources/supported-cameras.md) updates,\n"
"- [many other automation tools](./contribute/workflows.md) to help maintainability and\n"
"  debugging,\n"
"- a much reduced [code complexity](https://github.com/aurelienpierreeng/ansel#code-analysis),\n"
"- a written [design protocol](./contribute/design.md) and\n"
"  [triage rules](./contribute/triaging.md), so decisions can be checked instead of guessed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:82
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All this may sound cryptic to most users. It just means the maximum was made to help\n"
"stability and debugging, even for contributors who are not familiar with the code base,\n"
"therefore reducing the [bus factor](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bus_factor).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/donate.md:83
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You can be a part of that"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:88
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The kind of individuals that have the professional skills mentionned above tend to find\n"
"well-payed and stable job opportunities. If they are already practicing their skills\n"
"professionally all week long, chances are they want to rest from them on the spare time.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:94
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That's _very_ bad news for open-source/libre applications because it means they are left\n"
"with random contributions from amateurs, resulting in a long-known problem: open-source\n"
"applications are the half-baked, lower-end alternatives to their commercial counterparts,\n"
"being open somehow making it tolerable to a minority of users who value privacy over\n"
"getting their job done.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:98
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"__Open-source needs to pay well to attract skilled engineers, in order to produce\n"
"industry-grade applications__. It's really not rocket science: people need to pay their\n"
"bills first. Then perhaps work on cool stuff if they can. Not the other way around.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:103
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"__By financing Ansel, you are making it possible for the maintainer to put the required\n"
"time on fixing things properly and on solving your actual problems, without having to live\n"
"in financial stress.__ You are also giving other engineers incentives to do the same in\n"
"other projects by demonstrating it is possible.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:106
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"__You are contributing to a culture of fair work retribution in open-source__, which too\n"
"often relies on exploiting free labour and precariat.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:108
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You can donate through [Liberapay](https://liberapay.com/jiyone/donate).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:110
#: content/community/where-is-the-maps-module.md:198
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:77
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:93
#: content/community/may-somebody-help-with-the-development-of.md:116
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Thank you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:120
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"_Note:_ Ansel was founded by Aurélien Pierre, who worked on Darktable from the end of 2018 —\n"
"author of the darktable UCS 22 color space, of modules like filmic, tone equalizer, color\n"
"balance, diffuse & sharpen and lens blur, and of the scene-referred workflow, in addition\n"
"of having refactored the GUI code to allow user-defined theming. Ansel was forked from\n"
"Darktable 4.0 when its development effort dispersed into peripheral features whose cost —\n"
"in maintenance, in usability, in working conditions — nobody was accounting for\n"
"([the full story](./contribute/pact.md)). The project is now carried by its current\n"
"maintainer, whom this page supports.\n"
msgstr ""

