msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The original address was `https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/problem-importing-from-network-location`.\n"
"You can check this copy against the [snapshot in the Internet Archive](https://web.archive.org/web/20250120192941/https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/problem-importing-from-network-location).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:28
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **Vintage Lens Lover** on 2025-01-08.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I'm trying import photos from an SMB share on my NAS, however, no network locations show up while trying to import on my Linux Mint 22 workstation, even though I'm properly logged into the share and can access it from the file browser. On the other hand, my older PC (running Mint 21.3) has no problem doing the same thing and the network locations show up underneath the computer's local resources. Both instances are using \"Ansel-0.0.0+980.ga329ee63-x86_64.AppImage\". Any ideas what's going wrong?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:34
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:46
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:52
#: content/community/windows-7.md:94
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Vintage Lens Lover** — 2025-01-10\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:36
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I have now also tried Linux Mint Debian Edition 6 on the same machine, that works, but Ansel does not see the network shares in Mint 22.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:40
#: content/community/shortcut-mapping-missing.md:44
#: content/community/windows-7.md:86
#: content/community/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support.md:35
#: content/community/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support.md:49
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Aurélien Pierre** — 2025-01-10\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:42
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You need to install the GVFS packages for your system, noticeably the relevant SMB driver for GVFS. SMB networks have been confirmed to work with Ansel on Ubuntu and PopOS. GVFS provides the abstraction layer and handles the I/O through its own drivers, Ansel simply connects to that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:48
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I think I had already checked that but I will check again, thanks.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:54
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I had these packages installed:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:56
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "gvfs\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:58
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "gvfs-backends\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:60
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "gvfs-common\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:62
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "gvfs-daemon\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:64
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "gvfs-fuse\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:66
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "gvfs-libs\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:68
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I think gvfs-backends handles the SMB stuff. I can also access my KeePassXC database which is a gvfs SMB link.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:72
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:90
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:102
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**siamak** — 2025-05-20\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:74
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I have the very same problem with Darktable and Ansel with many linux distro. The only linux that seems to work for me out of the box is MX Linux. Too bad no one seems to want to give the solution to this issue. It does limit my linux choices for these apps. BTW, I came to like MX for ease of use and features.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:78
#: content/community/problem-importing-from-network-location.md:96
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
