msgid "Cheers for the info ﻿@Lukas﻿ I was going off the screenshot on the Ansel homepage\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:192
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**erik** — 2023-06-20\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:194
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hi! I have problems with the segmentation faults too. I haven't manage to solve it (properly), but I have narrowed it down a bit:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:198
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1.  It appears to be an issue when building Ansel with newer versions of clang. It seems to compile without issues with the build tools that is packaged with Apple Command Line Tools 14.2 or older. One quick fix is to downgrade you Apple Command Line Tools to version 14.2, but this is quite annoying as Apple is very eager to upgrade them again to the latest version.\n"
"2.  The segmentation fault only happens when the optimisation flag is set (-O1, -O2, -O3, etc). If the optimisation flag is removed, the file (iop_profile.c) compiles without issues on newer versions of clang.\n"
"3.  According to git bisect, the compiler has issues with the changes introduced in this commit: [https://github.com/aurelienpierreeng/ansel/commit/db783b2c6c13f362297632a72f28f021696c90c1](https://github.com/aurelienpierreeng/ansel/commit/db783b2c6c13f362297632a72f28f021696c90c1). There might be other commits as well, but this is the first one that breaks when trying to compile iop_profile.c\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:200
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I will try to look into it, but I am not an expert in C by any means. At the moment I am just building with Apple Command Line Tools 14.2 and call it a day. But this is a fix, not a solution. I will upload a new build ([here](https://www.qwd.no/ansel.html)) for intel Macs later today.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:202
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "EDIT: Developer Tools -\\> Command Line Tools\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:206
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Laurent Perraut** — 2023-06-20\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:208
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hi ﻿@isaac﻿ , I don't have an Intel mac at hand currently, I cannot test at the moment. I get Ansel compliled on my arm mac using xcode cli tools version 14.3.1. As soon I get access to an Intel mac I'll try.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:212
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:238
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:262
#: content/community/custom-module-groups-in-darkroom.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**isaac** — 2023-06-21\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:214
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hi All,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:216
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I've managed to track down the Segmentation Fault issue after commenting sections of code in the iop_profile.c file and slowing adding methods back one at a time.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:218
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "It's caused by \\_\\_DT_CLONE_TARGETS\\_\\_\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:220
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "It seems the Mac c compiler doesn't like the 'target_clones' attribute. Updating darktable.h to ignore this for Mac allows me to compile cleanly.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:222
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Line 129 changed\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ql-syntax)
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:223
#, no-wrap
msgid "#if __has_attribute(target_clones) && !defined(_WIN32) && !defined(NATIVE_ARCH)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:228
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ql-syntax)
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:229
#, no-wrap
msgid "#if __has_attribute(target_clones) && !defined(_WIN32) && !defined(__APPLE__) && !defined(NATIVE_ARCH)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:234
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "﻿@Laurent Perraut﻿ you would have been skipping this because of the M1 architecture\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:240
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I also managed to use ﻿@Laurent Perraut﻿ 's ./3_make_hb_ansel_package.sh script to create an app. Though instead of updating graphicsmagick as suggested in the BUILD_hb.txt\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:242
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I just created a 'naughty' symlink for missing libtiff.6.dylib ﻿🔨﻿\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ql-syntax)
#: content/community/ansel-on-mac.md:243
