#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/question-about-the-behavior-of-the.md:28
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **koslowj** on 2025-01-25.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/question-about-the-behavior-of-the.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In the darkroom, the space bar causes the next picture to be displayed. If the filmstrip is visible, both the last image and the now current one are then selected. In particular, rating the current image automatically also overwrites the rating of the previous image. The analogous phenomenon occurs when using the back-key, just in the other direction. Is this the intended behavior? Sometimes I like to rate all the pictures of a directory by stepping through them from start to finish. To maximise the view, I prefer to hide the filmstrip. But then I have no way of stepping forward or backwards, as the arrow-keys don't do the job.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/question-about-the-behavior-of-the.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Jiyone** — 2025-01-25\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/question-about-the-behavior-of-the.md:36
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "> Is this the intended behavior?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/question-about-the-behavior-of-the.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "No it's not, an there are many other things happening about the filmstrip ﻿﻿😅﻿﻿:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/question-about-the-behavior-of-the.md:42
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- Removing images from the library will remove any picture selected AND the one currently open.\n"
"- On the contrary, doing **image \\> rotate \\> 90° (counter) clockwise** will turn selected pictures EXCEPT the one currently open even if selected.\n"
"- BUT doing **edit \\> past history** on several images works as intended (the currently opened picture is safe if it's not selected).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/question-about-the-behavior-of-the.md:44
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The filmstrip is a mini lighttable, and the lighttable will need to be rewritten. Remember that Ansel is \"work in progress\" and things can appear broken overnight.\n"
msgstr ""

