#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/community/gamut-mapping.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gamut mapping"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/gamut-mapping.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The original address was `https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/gamut-mapping`.\n"
"You can check this copy against the [snapshot in the Internet Archive](https://web.archive.org/web/20250120180634/https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/gamut-mapping).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/gamut-mapping.md:28
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **Massimo** on 2025-01-06.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/gamut-mapping.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Using Sony proprietary raw converter (Imaging Edge), but I remember to have seen something similar with Canon DPP, raw files converted to sRGB or AdobeRGB look different (even without out of sRGB gamut colors in the scene). I think this is due to different gamut mapping between native camera color space and sRGB or Adobe RGB.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/gamut-mapping.md:32
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This behavior made me think about the fact that gamut mapping curves are out of user control.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/gamut-mapping.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Back to Ansel, would it make sense to have a module that allows to control gamut compression, much like filmic RGB does with respect to luminance?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/gamut-mapping.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Aurélien Pierre** — 2025-01-06\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/gamut-mapping.md:40
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You already have parametric gamut compression in color calibration. This will desaturate colors based on their chroma, using a power function. This was put there because, anyway, chromatic adaptation transform can and will push valid colors outside of gamut, especially the crazy LED blue.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/gamut-mapping.md:42
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "But ultimately, gamut is defined by color spaces which are defined by color profiles, and I believe that should be handled automatically when dealing with color conversions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/gamut-mapping.md:46
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Massimo** — 2025-01-06\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/gamut-mapping.md:48
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Thanks, I've found it in the CAT tab.\n"
msgstr ""

