#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:53
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The catalog is an SQLite database, you can use it the same with Ansel, no matter the OS. You can start Ansel with any config directory you want, even hosted on the Windows partition, with `ansel --configdir /path/to/your/config`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:55
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now, the issue will be that all the pathes to images will be referenced from the Windows perspective (`C:\\\\non-sense\\etc`), which will not be resolved from Linux. All in all, you would better write XMPs from Windows (menu Run -\\> Save all developments to XMP), then import the images from their folders from Linux.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Same with Linux, when you are done with an edit, save all developments to XMP.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To synchronize each Windows/Linux database with XMP, you have again the command into the Run menu.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:63
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**ariznaf** — 2023-03-27\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:65
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Thank you for the reply.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:67
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I have been making tests, it is possible to change new location of each import session, you can select it and all the paths in that session are updated, but that is not a thing you want to do each time you switch between Windows and Linux sesion.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:69
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "It seems a flaw in the design of the program to save absolute paths to the photo files, relatives paths and a import location would make it easier to move files around or access the same database from several computers.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:71
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In lightrom you create import directories and when you move a directory you only have to change the location of that directory and all files that depend on it get updated.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:75
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The solution seems to be to have two databases and use .xmp sidecar files to update changes. I will have to try.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:81
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Aurélien Pierre** — 2023-03-28\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:83
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "First of all, dt was designed for Unix-like systems, and was only ported to Windows much later.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:85
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Then, using relative pathes alone will most likely not fix problems of cross-platform filesystem compatibility. In fact, several parts of the code handling filenames and pathes have 2 variants, one for Unix-like and another for Windows. There is also the issue that Linux uses UTF-8 encoding while Windows still uses ISO something, which is a never-ending source of filename bugs for non-latin characters.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:87
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Having 2 DB is slightly annoying but more robust overall.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:91
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**ariznaf** — 2023-03-29\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:95
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Yes, as It is now, It Will be better yo have separate databases.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:97
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "But path related problems have been solved long time ago.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:99
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "There is a posix compliant library in Windows for accesing files and for having no problem with paths. All you have to do is use a function to convert Linux path strings before doing the file system call that works in Windows and Linux.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:101
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "But in a program already coded with thousands of lines It may be difficult to change It.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/may-i-open-the-catalog-from-linux-and.md:103
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "May be something yo have un mind in a new development (vkdt?).\n"
msgstr ""

