#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Muted contrast and filmic "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The original address was `https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/muted-contrast-and-filmic`.\n"
"No crawler ever captured this particular thread, so the text below — taken straight from the forum database — is the only copy left.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **Pedro Rodríguez** on 2023-04-13.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This is a question for @Aurélien Pierre.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "At some point in the chat you told me that artificially extending the DR of filmic puts stress on the interpolation and may produce inverted curves. Also, that filmic will be mapped to black point compensation at some point. I understood from this that filmic should just be treated as a more technical module, the display transform, and for artistic choices we should use tone eq and color balance RGB.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "After your recommendation, I'm reading the \"Color correction handbook\", and after going through the chapter on contrast, I was a bit unsure how to best create a lower contrast, muted look. Talking about highlights, the author says that they can generally be anywhere between 60-100%. If say I want my hl around the 70% mark (i know scopes are broken, I'm using my eyes, but just as a reference) what's the best way to achieve this?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:35
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I've tried pushing and pulling the luminance sliders in color balance, but such big shifts tend to reduce contrast quite a bit. Doing it via tone eq also hasn't yielded the best results. So far the best look comes from raising the white relative exposure in filmic carefully until the highlights are where i want them, then using tone equalizer and/or color balance RGB.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What is your take?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I will need a RAW file and a picture of the target look here.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:47
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Pedro Rodríguez** — 2023-04-13\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:49
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let's take this example of an indoor shot. One version is your typical exposure adjustment and filmic auto levels. It works great for me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The other is the same in terms of exposure (+1.970 EV), but went crazy with white relative exposure in filmic (+16EV). So that the curve wouldn't break, I reduced contrast in the look tab to 0.800. Then, following the recommendations of the Color correction handbook, I lowered the power in color balance RGB to -13.37% and raised my shadows by 100%.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:53
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here is the raw file:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:55
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1s2_6y5ErnIH--9sKqmxo-tqpaTNcqEcq/view?usp=share_link\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Pedro Rodríguez** — 2023-04-14\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/muted-contrast-and-filmic.md:61
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Found the better solution, I think. Reduce contrast in color balance RGB and bring shadows down with offset and shadows luminance sliders. It also has the added bonus of being able to control the contrast fulcrum in the masking tab.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid " Gtk-WARNING **: Theme parsing error: gtk.css"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The original address was `https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css`.\n"
"No crawler ever captured this particular thread, so the text below — taken straight from the forum database — is the only copy left.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **Aurélien Pierre** on 2023-06-07.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "If you launch either Darktable or Ansel from the terminal, you will get a bunch of lines like :\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ql-syntax)
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:30
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(ansel:67698): Gtk-WARNING **: 23:41:46.739: Theme parsing error: gtk.css:199:34: The :inconsistent pseudo-class is deprecated. Use :indeterminate instead.\n"
"(ansel:67698): Gtk-WARNING **: 23:41:46.742: Theme parsing error: gtk.css:1649:16: '-gtk-icon\n"
"-size' is not a valid property name\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The 2 important parts here are :\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:40
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- **WARNING**: computer programs have 3 levels of messages (info, warning, error). Only errors are blocking, warnings are nothing more than that (usually meaning that developers did something ugly but still sort-of working), and can be disregarded by end-users,\n"
"- **gtk.css**: this file is the main stylesheet provided by the desktop theme installed on the desktop environment, which is outside of the scope of Ansel and Darktable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:42
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This warning means that the Adwaita dark theme uses invalid or outdated styling statements that Gtk fails to decode (despite being the default Gnome theme). Ansel and Darktable use this desktop theme to initialize the GUI styling of the application (then apply their customizations on top), which is why the warning appears here, but there is ultimately nothing that can be done in the scope of either project to fix it, and that's something you need to report to the author of the theme.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:46
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Si vous lancez soit Darktable soit Ansel depuis le terminal, vous obtiendrez une paire de lignes du genre : \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:54
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Les deux parties importantes ici sont : \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- **WARNING (avertissement)** : les programmes informatiques ont 3 niveaux de messages (info, avertissement, erreur). Seules les erreurs sont bloquantes, les avertissements ne sont rien d'autre que cela (indiquant généralement que les développeurs ont fait quelque chose de sale mais tout de même globalement fonctionnel), et peuvent être ignorés par les utilisateurs finaux,\n"
"- **gtk.css** : ce fichier est la feuille de style principale fournie par le thème installé sur l'environnement de bureau, qui est hors du champ d'Ansel et Darktable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Cet avertissement signifie que le thème de bureau Adwaita sombre utilise des clauses de style invalides ou obsolètes que Gtk échoue à décoder (bien qu'étant le thème par défaut de Gnome). Ansel et Darktable utilisent ce thème du bureau pour initialiser le style de l'interface graphique de l'application (puis appliquent leurs personnalisations par dessus), ce qui explique pourquoi cet avertissement apparaît ici, mais en bout de ligne, il n'y a rien qui puisse être fait au niveau de ces deux projets pour régler le problème, et c'est quelque chose que vous devriez rapporter à l'auteur du thème.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:63
#: content/community/what-features-does-lighttable-filmstrip.md:104
#: content/community/what-features-does-lighttable-filmstrip.md:148
#: content/community/what-features-does-lighttable-filmstrip.md:176
#: content/community/what-features-does-lighttable-filmstrip.md:202
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**ariznaf** — 2023-06-12\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:65
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "May be that theme is a bit old or deprecated and it is time to change the default theme for another one?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/-gtk-warning-theme-parsing-error-gtk-css.md:71
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adwaita is the base and default theme maintained by the Gnome team, which happens to overlap a lot with the Gtk team, so I would assume it to be closely updated.\n"
msgstr ""

