#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-behavior-in-color-calibration.md:28
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **Jofial** on 2023-03-31.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-behavior-in-color-calibration.md:32
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I have detected a strange behavior in one of the Ansel modules. Specifically in the \"Color calibration\" module.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-behavior-in-color-calibration.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I have observed the following:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-behavior-in-color-calibration.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1.  I create a new instance of \"Color calibration\".\n"
"2.  I duplicate this instance for the B&W preset.\n"
"3.  I move the present over the \"color balance RGB\".\n"
"4.  I activate the present for B&W and in the \"History\" it is duplicated. Now I have two \"Color calibration\" with the same numeral \"1\".\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-behavior-in-color-calibration.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now if I don't like the result and I want to undo what I have done, I go to \"History\" select the initial instance of \"Color calibration\" and....\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-behavior-in-color-calibration.md:47
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The instance that I had duplicated is placed at the beginning of the module group \"color\".\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-behavior-in-color-calibration.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "If I compress the \"History\" to leave it as at the beginning, it is still at the beginning. If I activate it, this happens:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-behavior-in-color-calibration.md:55
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "It cannot be moved (Ctrl+Shift) and I can only delete it. Or close Ansel and reopen it. Only then the duplicated instance disappears.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-behavior-in-color-calibration.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I have tried the same with \"Exposure\" and it doesn't behave like that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-behavior-in-color-calibration.md:61
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "My Ansel is an AppImage, specifically:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-behavior-in-color-calibration.md:65
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "If I am doing something wrong, I would appreciate your corrections.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-behavior-in-color-calibration.md:67
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Note: I often duplicate this instance because I like B&W and this module is very versatile. The reason for placing it above the \"RGB color balance\" is so that it affects all the lower modules with respect to the modifications I have applied to them. It is the last module I use in the transformation to B&W.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-behavior-in-color-calibration.md:69
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Thanks for reading and trying\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-behavior-in-color-calibration.md:73
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Aurélien Pierre** — 2023-03-31\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-behavior-in-color-calibration.md:75
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "That looks like an unhandled case mixing history (old code) and pipeline reordering (fairly new code, 3 years old but not methodically tested).\n"
msgstr ""

