#: content/community/false-positive.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "False positive?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The original address was `https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/false-positive`.\n"
"No crawler ever captured this particular thread, so the text below — taken straight from the forum database — is the only copy left.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **Alessandro** on 2023-11-27.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Good morning, I would like to try using this software which seems very valid but there is no way to do it on my Windows PC as it is detected as a virus. Virustotal online also sees it like this in a couple of search engines...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:33
#: content/community/false-positive.md:41
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:45
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Aurélien Pierre** — 2023-11-28\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:35
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "It seems to be a reputation score fetched from databases, not a content analysis. Reputation means anybody able to report it is able to blacklist it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ".exe files are built every night on Github virtual server instances using Windows Server 2022. The code source is auditable, those virus-finding gentlemen can help themselves through the code…\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I ran the latest .Exe again and it gives another result : https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/a49810851b32b7a22c84d9bb9b5e8c90372b8b9f50de8b11326d4cd1c445c918?nocache=1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:45
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Meh…\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:49
#: content/community/false-positive.md:55
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Alessandro** — 2023-11-29\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Thank you. Yes, I was imaging that was just a false positive.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Nothing... I tried again with this: [ansel-1d3f83d-win64.exe](https://github.com/aurelienpierreeng/ansel/releases/download/v0.0.0/ansel-1d3f83d-win64.exe)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "but my antivirus complained again and quarantined it. I will have to wait for a \"lucky\" exe... :-(\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:65
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Can't you just bypass the antivirus and install anyway ? On my Windows, I have disabled all security features, they are annoying more than anything. Granted, I don't use Windows to open shady email attachments and I install pretty much nothing on it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:69
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**3dguy** — 2023-12-09\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:71
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "﻿@Aurélien Pierre﻿ I've went through the same issue when I distributed my 3D render farm management software. Lost a couple of customers due to the false positives. I can give details on how to fix this on your side, writing the details would take some work though, could you ping me here (or via email) if I should go ahead?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:75
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Alessandro** — 2023-12-12\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/false-positive.md:77
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Thank you but that won't be necessary. The main proposal of my initial post was just to alert the creator of this software and potentially other users of the problem. I think that no programmer likes the idea tha his creation is marked as a virus.\n"
msgstr ""

