#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Culling/Rating Images Workflow"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The original address was `https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/culling-rating-images-workflow`.\n"
"You can check this copy against the [snapshot in the Internet Archive](https://web.archive.org/web/20231001123557/https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/culling-rating-images-workflow).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:28
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **Joshua** on 2023-04-15.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hello all!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:32
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I was wondering if people wouldn't mind sharing how they assess a collection of new photos for which to work on further? (commonly called culling, but I will omit this term to avoid confusion with the removed \"Culling\" mode)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:36
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Personally, the most intuitive approach would be able to view each photo in a full screen, and then with keyboard shortcuts rate/reject photos, and move onto the next.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This almost works out-of-the-box in Ansel, but there's a quirk with photo selection.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:40
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The rating/reject shortcuts work on the \"Selected\" image (shown with a light grey highlight), however arrow keys do not change this \"Selected\" image they merely move the \"cursor\" to other images, at which point they can be selected with \"Space\".\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:44
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This leads me to use this workflow currently:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:46
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1\\. Adjust Lighttable to view 1 photo per row, press tab to remove panels.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:48
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2\\. Rate/reject/color the photo\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:50
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3\\. Press Space to unselect it\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:52
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "4\\. Move to the next photo with Right\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:54
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "5\\. Press Space to select it\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:56
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "6\\. Repeat from step 2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:62
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This is fairly cumbersome, and I do not like that if I've made a mistake with my Space select/unselect dance, I can end up with some other photo silently selected in the background and then I am performing invisible rating/rejection edits to it without realising.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:66
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Please let me know if I'm missing something here, or any alternative approaches people have.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:72
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Joshua\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:76
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Aurélien Pierre** — 2023-04-16\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:78
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The lighttable is currently undergoing cleanup and simplification, which I fear will end up in a complete rewrite, so there are transient annoyances like that for now.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:82
#: content/community/can-t-find-the-zoom-options-that-were.md:41
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Lukas** — 2023-04-17\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:84
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This is a similar problem, ﻿@omrihar﻿\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:88
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**cyberspeck** — 2023-05-12\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:90
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I face the same problem. And I would be interested to know (or contribute to) the future design of the lighttable view. For me, I feel like work in lighttable currently takes 3 times the effort it should take. Cheers, david\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:96
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Providing feedback in the thumbnails about stars, flags an other info would be great and would help, as you could immediately see the changes to classification.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:98
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lightroom has strong capabilities in that aspect, I think it would be a good model to follow.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:102
#: content/community/what-features-does-lighttable-filmstrip.md:78
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Steve** — 2023-06-10\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:104
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I concur. Ansel really needs a simple browser for viewing/zooming/rating files before import.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:108
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**cyberspeck** — 2023-10-09\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:112
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Any estimate when the lighttable will get its overhaul? Today it accidently marked a big numer of my photos as 'rejected' and I could not undo it without restoring an backup of the xmp files. Honestly, I don't trust Ansel to provide what I need for efficient and reliable culling right now.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:116
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Aurélien Pierre** — 2023-10-10\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:118
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How did you accidentally reject all the pictures ? Using the mouse or the keyboard ? Did Ctrl+Z work ?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:122
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**cyberspeck** — 2023-10-10\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:124
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I was marking images using the mouse and pressing \"r\" to reject the photos which I wanted to delete. At one point Ansel did not longer reject them but a pop up said \"r not defined\" (or something similar). I don't know what exactly had happened at this point. I tried to get \"r\" working again by switching into darkroom mode and back, but it still didn't recognise \"r\". I then closed/restarted Ansel. By that time the undo history was gone, but only then when I continued to mark images I noticed that I had somehow marked more as rejected than I had intended. I'm not sure how it happened, but I the inconsistent behaviour probably led to me doing it without being aware.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:128
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Lukas** — 2023-10-11\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/culling-rating-images-workflow.md:130
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
