#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/community/ctrl-key-doesn-t-work-for-selecting-shapes.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ctrl-Key doesn't work for selecting shapes in the retouch module"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ctrl-key-doesn-t-work-for-selecting-shapes.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The original address was `https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/ctrl-key-doesn-t-work-for-selecting-shapes`.\n"
"You can check this copy against the [snapshot in the Internet Archive](https://web.archive.org/web/20250514051330/https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/ctrl-key-doesn-t-work-for-selecting-shapes).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ctrl-key-doesn-t-work-for-selecting-shapes.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In version 43e3443 the retouch module shows another small problem: in order to repeatedly use one of the given shapes, one is supposed to press Ctrl when selecting the shape. Presently this does not work anymore.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ctrl-key-doesn-t-work-for-selecting-shapes.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Aurélien Pierre** — 2025-01-20\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ctrl-key-doesn-t-work-for-selecting-shapes.md:36
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "It's not a problem, the special behaviours triggered by \"silly key shortcut + mouse click\" regarding masks are being removed. Since masks are supposed to be drawn, and drawing devices are Wacom tablets but not keyboards, those silly modes are migrated to a toolbar that will be clickable with a pen.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ctrl-key-doesn-t-work-for-selecting-shapes.md:42
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I'm not quite convinced. General masks, OK, but having to use a Wacom tablet just for efficiently fixing some blemishes in a portrait or dust spots that require just circular shapes seems overkill. Can the user at least re-create those short-cuts?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ctrl-key-doesn-t-work-for-selecting-shapes.md:48
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Wacom tablets are only a particular kind of pointing device. Pointing devices should not require keyboard interaction for typical user events. Here, the Ctrl+click feature is well hidden to users, and is used as a workaround for lack of proper mask GUI allowing to quickly toggle ON/OFF the mask editing mode.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ctrl-key-doesn-t-work-for-selecting-shapes.md:50
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Retouch masks are general masks. There is only one library for all masks in the software. But the continuous editing mode is a special case inside a special case, inside generic masks. Special cases are being removed, because they are a liability (plus the code has been copy-pasted everywhere, it's a mess).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ctrl-key-doesn-t-work-for-selecting-shapes.md:52
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Masks are currently being reworked entirely. See https://github.com/aurelienpierreeng/ansel/issues/418\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Versions - Install or Appimage?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The original address was `https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/versions-install-or-appimage`.\n"
"No crawler ever captured this particular thread, so the text below — taken straight from the forum database — is the only copy left.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **gomi** on 2024-03-16.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I'm currently running Ansel on an Appimage. The last update was early January. Is it felt that the pace of updates has slowed sufficiently for a full installation to be more appropriate? I'm on Arch Linux so it would be the AUR repository version, which is currently carrying the same date as the Appimage.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I have three questions but not sure which context to ask them in, Appimage or full install. I'll mention them here but await pointers:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:35
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1.  Imported a newly downloaded folder of images and began processing in Ansel. One image is now a single black rectangle in Lighttable view. It starts off as a totally black image in Darkroom but the image returns if I scroll in slightly. is this a known problem? {Edit: the exported Jpeg is perfect, so the 'problem' only exists visually in Ansel}\n"
"2.  I can't see a way to import a new watermark in either PNG or SVG format. There is no directory .config/Ansel/, only the .config/ansel/\n"
"3.  There are several folders already imported and images processed in my old darktable config files .config/darktable/ but they are mostly DT 4.2 or later. Is it better to import them into Ansel as raw files and re-process them or are my efforts likely to persist if I pull the DT DB files into .config/ansel/?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "TIA,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Mike\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:45
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "> Imported a newly downloaded folder of images and began processing in Ansel. One image is now a single black rectangle in Lighttable view. It starts off as a totally black image in Darkroom but the image returns if I scroll in slightly. is this a known problem? {Edit: the exported Jpeg is perfect, so the 'problem' only exists visually in Ansel}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:47
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "It's a known issue. To mitigate it until it's fixed, hit global menu -\\> Run -\\> clear pipeline caches when it appears.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:49
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "> I can't see a way to import a new watermark in either PNG or SVG format. There is no directory .config/Ansel/, only the .config/ansel/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Just create that directory and add your watermarks if it's not created automatically.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:53
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "> There are several folders already imported and images processed in my old darktable config files .config/darktable/ but they are mostly DT 4.2 or later. Is it better to import them into Ansel as raw files and re-process them or are my efforts likely to persist if I pull the DT DB files into .config/ansel/?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:55
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ansel is compatible with Darktable up to 4.0. For editings made with Darktable 4.2, you may loose your settings for filmic and highlights reconstruction modules.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Ansel is still not considered stable as of now.**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:61
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**gomi** — 2024-03-16\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/versions-install-or-appimage.md:63
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Thanks Aurelien (and apologies for not finding how to type the accent on the e). That's all a lot easier than I'd imagined.\n"
msgstr ""

