#, no-wrap
msgid "Strange compile problems with Lua and clang compiler"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The original address was `https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and`.\n"
"No crawler ever captured this particular thread, so the text below — taken straight from the forum database — is the only copy left.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **Maurizio Paglia** on 2023-11-28.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I switched to Suse Tumbleweed and compiled Ansel on my own.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "No problem detected with my previous Suse Leap 15.4 distro.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now seems Ansel cannot detect Lua on my system so Lua support is not included.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:35
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Moreover I receive an error (or advice?) message saying a clang compiler cannot be found despite the fact clang is duly installed on my system and Ansel is compiled and installed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Can someone help?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:47
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The CLang issue may be linked to https://github.com/aurelienpierreeng/ansel/commit/91bac822b26f2b35cfaa6761bf7b13b1aface503\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:49
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ansel looks for Lua 5.3 exactly, if I recall correctly, it doesn't accept anything older or newer. But anyway, since the Lua overlay is looking for a binary called \\`darktable\\` (it's hard-coded), it has never worked since renaming to Ansel and that needs to be changed upstream.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:53
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Faber** — 2023-12-22\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:55
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Do you know what it would take to get lua scripts working in Ansel?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I really appreciate what you have done with Ansel, and have been wanting to switch to it for awhile. Darktable is now grabbing/stealing global window manager keybindings (super key) and that was a final straw for me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I've grown accustom to a couple workflow related scripts and would like to get them working before jumping fully into Ansel. I'm by no means a developer, but if the required fixes are on the lua side only, I might be able to hack it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:61
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Any pointers would be greatly appreciated.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:65
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Maurizio Paglia** — 2024-01-01\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:67
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I have lua 5.4.6 installed on my distro and now Ansel can compile with lua support.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:69
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Some scripts works out of the box, other cannot and other (in my case photils.lua) cause a segmentation fault.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:73
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Maurizio Paglia** — 2024-01-03\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:75
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Recompiled Ansel right now from sources and lua support disappeared again... sorry...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:79
#: content/community/combien-de-partitions-pour-ansel.md:51
#: content/community/guided-filter-box-mean-x-runs-10-times.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Aurélien Pierre** — 2024-01-15\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/strange-compile-problems-with-lua-and.md:81
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The default CMake build options don't enable Lua support by default because Lua is currently wonky (as you saw, some plugins work, some make the app crash). You can manually enable it using CMake options at building.\n"
msgstr ""

