#, no-wrap
msgid "Color Label"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/color-label.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The original address was `https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/color-label`.\n"
"You can check this copy against the [snapshot in the Internet Archive](https://web.archive.org/web/20240422133715/https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/color-label).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/color-label.md:28
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **Steve** on 2023-12-18.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/color-label.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The XMP specification calls for the \\<xmp:Label\\> property.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/color-label.md:32
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The XMP file Ansel creates contains only a private \\<darktable:colorlabels\\> property.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/color-label.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Is it possible to also add the \\<xmp:Label\\>colorXXX\\</xmp:Label\\> to the generated XMP file ?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/color-label.md:36
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This would allow for any application to be able to read the Color Label.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/color-label.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This would be the same as the currently generated Star Number \\<xmp:Rating\\>numberXXX\\</xmp:Rating\\> that is already generated by Ansel as per XMP specification.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/color-label.md:40
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I think it would be very helpful if there are other properties that could also be generated using the XMP specification, so as to allow any application that reads XMP files, to at least have a fighting chance in pulling as much data as possible.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/color-label.md:44
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Aurélien Pierre** — 2024-01-27\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/color-label.md:46
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I have been told that dt re-implemented standard color labels because the standard ones are mutually-exclusive, while the private dt ones can use more than one label at a time.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/color-label.md:48
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I will have to check all that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/color-label.md:50
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Using XMP tags that other applications can understand is a doubled-edged sword, as always, because then other apps can mess up with your data without user knowing it. Again, needs some serious assessment of needs, constraints, requirements and safety.\n"
msgstr ""

