#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/trojan-in-latest-release-ansel-0-0-0-1333.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **Ed Mathis** on 2025-02-21.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/trojan-in-latest-release-ansel-0-0-0-1333.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This morning I went to the github nightly builds and downloaded ansel-0.0.0+1333.g9242d5a5-win64.exe. When I tried to move the file to my storage directory Windows Defender immediately quarantined the file. Looking further, it reported a trojan embedded in the file. Click on the title of this posting to see a copy of Defender's report.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/trojan-in-latest-release-ansel-0-0-0-1333.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Is this a false positive?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/trojan-in-latest-release-ansel-0-0-0-1333.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**topoldo** — 2025-02-21\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/trojan-in-latest-release-ansel-0-0-0-1333.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Me, too! Windows 11 Pro 24H2. Ansel version: sama as Ed Mathis.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/trojan-in-latest-release-ansel-0-0-0-1333.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Topoldo\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/trojan-in-latest-release-ansel-0-0-0-1333.md:49
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Well, all I can tell you is I didn't put a trojan in there and my Github account hasn't been breached, which means no malicious code was injected there. If you got the .exe straight from Github, that should be fine. Now, if you got the .exe from somewhere else, I can't guarantee it has not been tampered with.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/trojan-in-latest-release-ansel-0-0-0-1333.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You could try from an earlier version too, see if the antivirus catches it too. Anyway, those use binary fingerprints to detect viruses, so false-positives happened in the past and will happen again.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/trojan-in-latest-release-ansel-0-0-0-1333.md:55
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Ed Mathis** — 2025-02-21\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/trojan-in-latest-release-ansel-0-0-0-1333.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I got it straight from Github this morning, where I always get the updates. The previous version -1329 downloaded and installed just fine with no warnings. Dunno...... I'll try again after Windows Defender undergoes a few more updates that may solve the false positive.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/trojan-in-latest-release-ansel-0-0-0-1333.md:63
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "There are 65/70 antivirus that pass clean… https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/b7685065159d284931f8188c1947c37b6dd32d6b5d161ed55536865dc490ca2e\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/trojan-in-latest-release-ansel-0-0-0-1333.md:65
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "But I tested all Ansel versions since 1329, and they all trigger 3 to 5 antiviruses in the pack. It's been seen before…\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/trojan-in-latest-release-ansel-0-0-0-1333.md:69
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Aurélien Pierre** — 2025-02-22\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/trojan-in-latest-release-ansel-0-0-0-1333.md:71
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For the record, Windows antivirus has an history of detecting Wacatac malware everywhere: https://www.reddit.com/r/antivirus/comments/14bhb6u/trojanwin32wacatacbml_trojanscriptwacatacbml/\n"
msgstr ""

