#, no-wrap
msgid "ICC v4 monitor profile support"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The original address was `https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support`.\n"
"No crawler ever captured this particular thread, so the text below — taken straight from the forum database — is the only copy left.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **Massimo** on 2025-01-09.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "When system display profile is an ICC version 4, darkroom visualization is noticeable darker, see attached comparison image.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ansel version is 0.0.0+984~gbe2369ae and operating system is Windows 10.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Why are you using ICC v4 ? They bring no improvement over v2, which explains why many software didn't bother implementing support. More details : https://www.argyllcms.com/doc/iccgamutmapping.html\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support.md:41
#: content/community/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Massimo** — 2025-01-10\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Version 4 is the default of my calibration tool from x-rite, but actually in my current workflow I do not have any constraint that prevents me to use a version 2 profile.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support.md:45
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "That being said, a version 4 support is likely more future proof as this version in constantly updated from ICC consortium, for example HDR support has been recently added.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "HDR support is the ICCmax version, not v4 as far as I'm aware. ICC v4 is not supported by ArgyllCMS (see link above), therefore not supported by Display Cal. The ICC workflow being printer-centric, HDR is irrelevant here. Anyway, HDR workflows moved to OCIO/ACES.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support.md:53
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "All I can say is ICC v2 is supported everywhere, many devs & projects didn't bother with v4, and ICCmax is supported nowhere and not planned for adoption for apps that need HDR. So, just stick to good old ICC v2, the future of ICC is 30 years ago.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "My understanding was that with the adoption of cicpTag in version 4.4 (2022), that links to ITU or SMPTE specification, ICC profiles would be used for still and video HDR contents on computers.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/icc-v4-monitor-profile-support.md:61
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "From your reply, I'm learning that this would probably not be the case.\n"
msgstr ""

