#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/drawn-mask-covers-entire-screen-what-am-i.md:80
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I usuallly do not use the left menu for selections, just when I need to delete a figure or something.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/drawn-mask-covers-entire-screen-what-am-i.md:82
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Usually you create the selection in the right menu.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/drawn-mask-covers-entire-screen-what-am-i.md:86
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "But you can create it in the left an select one of the figures created to be applied to a module, they are the same, at the left you see al figures created for any module and grouped for figures used in a module.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/drawn-mask-covers-entire-screen-what-am-i.md:88
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "It seems a bit confuse, I know.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/drawn-mask-covers-entire-screen-what-am-i.md:94
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "> I'm pretty sure the \"Mask Opacity\" in the upper left is totally unrelated to the \"Mask Opacity\" that's found in \"Mask Refinement\" section of the module (right sidebar).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/drawn-mask-covers-entire-screen-what-am-i.md:96
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "There are several opacities here, the masking logic is really messy.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/drawn-mask-covers-entire-screen-what-am-i.md:98
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You have shapes, drawn from several methods (circle, ellipse, path, pen), that get aggregated in groups (possibly using boolean operations) to define masks. Groups can themselves be aggregated in hierarchical groups. The highest level of mask group is the module level, which is targeted by the opacity slider you see in the masking options (refinement) in the module. While the global opacity slider in the header toolbar targets the group to which the currently-selected shape belongs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/drawn-mask-covers-entire-screen-what-am-i.md:100
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The joys and wonders of multi-layered masking code hacked again every 2 years since 2014 to avoid a anxiety-triggering rewrite…\n"
msgstr ""

